    "observations": "In both of the clearest mosaics the two front roofs on either side of the narrow opening have a separate second rank of warm tiled roof shapes behind a dark transverse break. On the lane-side part of 493 the visible individual front pitch covers approximately 9–12 m along the street and 7–10 m in depth. Calibration to the street photo includes eaves overhang, roof-height parallax, and lateral registration uncertainty. The independent middle and east portions of 493 continue along the street. The aerial image alone does not establish which interior door belongs to which roof.",
    "local_reference_samples": "Pixel coordinates in roof-grid-base-*.jpg map to local metres by X=(u−270)/7, Y=(355−v)/7. The annotated two-by-two contact sheet groups the 2010, 2019, 2021 and 2025 acquisition records.",
    "clip_recommendation": "Keep all native material outside the photographed street-side volume. For a city test, use a component- or triangle-level cut of the identified west end of 493 and draw the original remainder, with the roof and row to the east preserved. Feature 4001 and all distinct courtyard features require independent evidence before changing them."
